        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-23T23:15:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, the best prefix for this file and these functions is _probably_ `typec_`. There are a few existing public functions with this name, and they tend to do kind of the same thing as these new functions: Update the state of one of the Type-C signals in a way that abstracts the port hardware away for the caller. I had previously suggested `pd_*`, but the functions here are not specific to PD.\n\nAs noted elsewhere, there already is a `typec_` function for setting the source current limit, and that\u0027s kind of a can of worms, but that shouldn\u0027t stop us from using a good naming convention otherwise.",
      "revId": "c19dfacc5282fd3e939479d672394b4108455c7a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
